  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "s01-flow",
      "intent": "the recurrence returns to the DQ-CTM thought stage, while encode and decode stay outside the loop",
      "claim": "ThinkSR end to end: encoder, windows, shared DQ-CTM ticks, decoder.",
      "narration": "The image is first encoded into a dense carrier, so spatial detail is available before reasoning starts. Windowing passes the carrier onward without turning the whole pipeline into a recurrent loop. The DQ-CTM thought process ticks repeatedly, and the same parameters are reused at each tick. Decoding happens after those shared ticks, so the recurrence belongs to the thought stage itself.",
