      "id": "s02-carrier",
      "intent": "the carrier equation first makes a dense feature field, then partitions that field into windows without dropping tokens",
      "claim": "\\mathbf{F}=\\mathcal{E}(\\mathbf{I}_{\\mathrm{LR}}),\\qquad \\mathbf{X}=\\mathcal{W}(\\mathbf{F})",
      "narration": "The encoder maps the low-resolution image into a dense feature field named F. The window operator then partitions that field into X for the thought process. The equation keeps F inside the window step, so every token comes from the dense carrier.",
